  "research_state": "Bootstrap coordinator state. Goal: TEST_ONLY_EXTRA_HIGH_LEAF_OVERRIDE. Investigate the optimal endpoint-zero discrete path Poincare inequality for every integer N >= 2 and real sequence x_0 = x_N = 0. Determine the sharp constant C_N, characterize all equality cases, and establish a rigorous quantitative stability estimate for near extremizers. No mathematical findings have yet been certified by child reports. Create exactly two complementary children, with weights 0.55 and 0.45. Child 1 pursues spectral eigenvalues, equality, and sharp stability. Child 2 pursues an elementary finite-sum proof, independent sharpness checks, and boundary verification. Each child has a three-round research plan; only its first round is authorized by the initial prompt. Child 1: Round 1 derives the complete Dirichlet spectrum, optimal constant, and equality classification; Round 2 establishes quantitative stability from the spectral gap, with precise deficit normalization; Round 3 investigates optimality of the stability coefficient, normalization conventions, and degenerate cases N = 2 and N = 3. Child 2: Round 1 develops a direct finite-sum or ground-state-transform proof of the sharp inequality and checks boundary contributions; Round 2 derives a quantitative near-extremizer estimate by elementary weighted telescoping and Cauchy-Schwarz methods, avoiding spectral decomposition; Round 3 audits all endpoint and small-N cases, compares the elementary estimates with the spectral conclusions, and resolves any remaining proof gaps. Candidate formulas to investigate, not yet accepted as established results: lambda_k = 4 sin^2(k*pi/(2*N)) for k = 1,...,N-1; C_N = 1/lambda_1; extremizers proportional to sin(pi*j/N); and a spectral stability coefficient involving lambda_2 - lambda_1 for N >= 3. The N = 2 case is one-dimensional and must not invoke a nonexistent second eigenvalue. Each round must produce one concise complete mathematical report, preferably below 1200 words, explicitly distinguishing proved statements from conjectures or incomplete arguments. No external data or software execution is required. All experimental leaves use GPT-6 Extra High. No claim of independent verification or external validation is authorized. The coordinator does not execute child research turns.",
